      "description": "Watch Portland Timbers vs Minnesota United FC highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 6, 2026. The clash between the Portland Timbers and Minnesota United on September 6, 2026, delivered a spectacle that will be remembered for its relentless pace and constant shifts in momentum. Both sides showed incredible offensive intent in a game where the lead never felt secure for long. A First-Half Scoring Frenzy Portland Timbers wasted no time establishing dominance in front of their home fans. The deadlock was broken in the 11th minute when Vincent Janssen calmly dispatched a penalty. The momentum stayed with the hosts, and in the 21st minute, a defensive mishap saw Drake Callender turn the ball into his own net. Portland looked to be running away with the contest when Vincent Janssen struck again in the 27th minute, assisted by David Da Costa , to make it 3-0. However, Minnesota United produced a spirited response before the break. Marcus Caldeira pulled one back in the 32nd minute following a setup by Joaquin Pereyra , and the deficit was trimmed further in the 38th minute when Anthony Markanich found the net thanks to Kelvin Yeboah . Despite a yellow card for Finn Surman in stoppage time, the visitors went into the interval with renewed hope after a breathless 45 minutes. Janssen Completes the Hat-Trick The second half began with high drama as Marcus Caldeira secured his brace in the 51st minute, remarkably bringing Minnesota level at 3-3. The parity lasted only four minutes, as Vincent Janssen clinical finishing saw him complete his hat-trick in the 55th minute, assisted by Ariel Lassiter . Portland extended their cushion to 5-3 in the 71st minute through Kristoffer Velde , who capitalized on an Antony assist shortly after coming on. As the clock ticked down, the intensity remained high with yellow cards shown to Jefferson Diaz and Morris Duggan . A late surge from Minnesota United saw Tomas Chancalay score in the 92nd minute, set up by Carlos Harvey , to create a nervous finale. Despite the late pressure, Portland Timbers held firm to secure all three points in a classic MLS encounter that featured nine goals and non-stop action."
